{"nodes": [{"id": "agents_agent_guide", "label": "AGENTS.md project instructions", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_content_from_sanity", "label": "Content comes from Sanity (no hardcoded copy)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "# Content comes from Sanity", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any user-facing sentence must become a schema field so editors can change copy without a code deploy."}, {"id": "agents_cache_components_rules", "label": "Cache Components rules (cacheComponents: true)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Cache Components rules", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Violating either constraint is a build error rather than a runtime bug, so the rules are enforced structurally: all reads in content.ts, perspective resolved above the cache boundary."}, {"id": "agents_sanityfetch_use_cache_rule", "label": "sanityFetch only inside 'use cache' scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "Cache Components rules #1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "sanityFetch calls cacheTag() and cacheLife() internally, which throw outside a cache scope; centralising call sites in sanity/lib/content.ts guarantees this."}, {"id": "agents_perspectivegate_pattern", "label": "PerspectiveGate route pattern (cookies above cache boundary)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "Cache Components rules #2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cookies()/headers() cannot be read inside 'use cache'; PerspectiveGate resolves the perspective above the boundary and threads it down as FetchOptions so it becomes part of the cache key. generateMetadata uses PUBLISHED directly to keep the document head in the static shell."}, {"id": "agents_where_things_go", "label": "Where things go (schema/queries/content/types/tags/resolve)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Where things go", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_no_dot_in_document_id", "label": "Never put a dot in a document _id", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sanity reads a dot as a path separator; path-prefixed documents are hidden from unauthenticated reads (same mechanism as drafts.*). The site fetches published content without a token, so a dotted ID renders in Studio but 404s for visitors. Use '-'."}, {"id": "agents_cache_tags_cover_dereferenced_types", "label": "Cache tags must cover dereferenced types", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The revalidate webhook invalidates by _type and knows nothing about references, so a query that dereferences author-> must also be tagged with person or it goes stale."}, {"id": "agents_headlines_are_portable_text", "label": "Headlines are Portable Text with accent marks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lime marker / green / rust accents are marks rendered by components/sanity/Headline.tsx so editors can move emphasis without code changes; never split into partA+highlight+partB strings."}, {"id": "agents_positional_numbering", "label": "Numbering derived from array position", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Numbers and anchors (legal sections, FAQ groups, funnel stages) are never stored so reordering in the Studio renumbers automatically."}, {"id": "agents_sanityimage_pipeline", "label": "Images via SanityImage with lqip + dimensions (IMAGE fragment)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SanityImage reads dimensions from the asset ref so next/image reserves space without a round trip; queries must project lqip and dimensions."}, {"id": "agents_singletons", "label": "Singleton documents (siteSettings, homePage, ...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Conventions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adding a singleton requires updating sanity/schemaTypes/index.ts, the Studio structure, and the presentation resolver."}, {"id": "agents_typegen_after_schema_change", "label": "Run npm run typegen after schema/query change", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "## Where things go", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "sanity_lib_content", "label": "sanity/lib/content.ts (cached reads)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "components_perspectivegate", "label": "components/PerspectiveGate.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_api_revalidate_route", "label": "app/api/revalidate/route.ts (Sanity webhook)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "A